From dfc02503e0e053dfa7cbd91e3bf5fdb746583fd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:19:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 166/202] drm/mediatek: mtk_dsi: Refuse transfers while the DSI
 is powered off

A transfer did not check that the DSI was powered on. On the JP2601,
systemd-backlight restores the brightness (DCS 51h) at ~17 s, before the
shell's first modeset at ~20 s, with the bootloader's video still
running. The transfer stopped that stream, brought the lanes up and set
lanes_ready. The first power-on then reprogrammed the PLL but skipped the
lane bring-up (D-PHY reset, ULPS exit) as already done, so the panel took
the LP init commands but showed nothing of the HS video, until a power
off and on cleared lanes_ready. After a power off the same path touches
registers with the clocks gated.

Return -ENODEV unless the DSI is powered on.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
index effff86a2..29a42ee62 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -1304,6 +1304,10 @@ static ssize_t mtk_dsi_host_transfer(struct mipi_dsi_host *host,
 	u32 dsi_mode;
 	int ret, i;
 
+	/* Not powered on: the bootloader's setup, or gated clocks */
+	if (!dsi->refcount)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	dsi_mode = readl(dsi->regs + DSI_MODE_CTRL);
 	if (dsi_mode & MODE) {
 		mtk_dsi_stop(dsi);
-- 
